        "mapping_rules": [
          "SUCCESS maps to a frozen object with ok true and value",
          "FAILURE maps to a frozen object with ok false and error",
          "All neutral non-constructor operations are exposed as both camelCase module callables and Result instance methods; success-option uses method toOption because ok is the required boolean discriminator, and constructors are module-only",
          "TypeScript extensions are camelCase module callables and never Result instance methods",
          "Compile-time types must not exceed runtime evidence",
          "ResultData is plain branch data; JSON, spread, assignment, and structured clone do not preserve Result methods",
          "Free Result operations accept ResultLike and every Result-valued output is a canonical local methodful wrapper",
          "Hydration reuses local wrappers and rewraps transport data or wrappers from another package copy",
          "Optional structured Failure projects as the Failure type, Failure constructor, isFailure guard, and governed bounded-validation limits without constraining Result<T,E>"
        ],
