        "mapping_rules": [
          "PyPI distribution resultsafe uses import root resultsafe and has no runtime dependencies",
          "SUCCESS maps to frozen slotted generic Ok(value) and FAILURE maps to frozen slotted generic Err(error)",
          "SOME maps to frozen slotted generic Some(value) and NONE maps to singleton NOTHING",
          "The 21 neutral non-constructor operations are exposed as both snake_case module callables and Result instance methods; constructors are module-only and TypeScript extensions are excluded",
          "ResultExtractionError.payload preserves the opposite branch payload by identity",
          "Pass-through branches reuse wrappers; constructed branches preserve payload references; callback counts, exceptions, transpose branches, laws, and shallow immutability follow Contract IR",
          "The package includes py.typed and is qualified with strict mypy and an isolated wheel consumer",
          "ResultData uses explicit discriminator dictionaries; dataclasses.asdict is not a transport conversion",
          "Pickle and copy preserve runtime dataclass behavior while explicit hydration restores runtime values from transport dictionaries",
          "Optional structured Failure projects as a frozen slotted dataclass with explicit to_failure_data conversion and does not constrain Result[T,E]"
